Subject: configure: a cross build for Darwin takes its release from the host triple

A cross build sets ac_sys_release to the empty string, so on Darwin the
"Darwin/[12][0-9].*" case that keeps _XOPEN_SOURCE and _POSIX_C_SOURCE
undefined never matches. pyconfig.h then defines both, <sys/socket.h> hides
sendfile(), and posixmodule.c fails to compile; probes run under those
defines also lose HAVE_CHROOT and HAVE_GETPAGESIZE. A native build reads the
release from uname -r. A cross build now reads the major release from the
host triple (x86_64-apple-darwin13 gives 13.0), which is the part every
Darwin/<release> case in configure looks at. Hosts other than Darwin keep
the empty release.

Upstreamable as is. Drop it when CPython's configure derives the release for
a Darwin cross build itself.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -4148,6 +4148,7 @@
        # ac_sys_system and ac_sys_release are used for setting
        # a lot of different things including 'define_xopen_source'
        # in the case statement below.
+	ac_sys_release=
 	case "$host" in
 	*-*-linux-android*)
 		ac_sys_system=Linux-android
@@ -4163,6 +4164,7 @@
 		;;
 	*-*-darwin*)
 		ac_sys_system=Darwin
+		ac_sys_release=`expr "$host_os" : 'darwin\([0-9][0-9]*\)'`.0
 		;;
 	*-gnu)
 		ac_sys_system=GNU
@@ -4181,7 +4183,6 @@
 		MACHDEP="unknown"
 		as_fn_error $? "cross build not supported for $host" "$LINENO" 5
 	esac
-	ac_sys_release=
     else
 	ac_sys_system=`uname -s`
 	if test "$ac_sys_system" = "AIX" \
